## 9. The end-to-end request journey in one story

Here is the full trace from the user pressing send all the way to the answer returning:

1. User types a question into the portal chat UI.
2. The UI creates a JSON request with message text and a session id.
3. The UI calls `POST https://{apim}.azure-api.net/chat`.
4. APIM checks CORS, enforces allowed origins, and applies rate-limits.
5. APIM logs request metadata and forwards the request to the Azure Function backend.
6. The Function validates the request payload.
7. The Function maps the browser session id to a Foundry conversation context.
8. The Function obtains a secure token using managed identity.
9. The Function sends the chat request to the Foundry Responses endpoint for the TicketDeflection application.
10. Foundry executes the TicketDeflection workflow and returns answer data.
11. The Function receives the Foundry response, cleans it up, and returns a simplified payload.
12. APIM forwards the Function response back to the browser.
13. The browser renders the assistant reply in the chat bubble.

